<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wuyuan Commandery</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">127 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wuyuan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/commandery">Commandery</a> was a frontier commandery of Han <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, created in 127 BCE on the great northern bend of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-river">Yellow River</a>, around modern Baotou in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inner-mongolia">Inner Mongolia</a>. Lying on the border with the steppe, it was repeatedly contested by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu</a> and later the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xianbei">Xianbei</a>, and the region was abandoned by the Chinese court at the end of the Han.</p></div>
